<title>CANADA: Canada new housing price index falls in Oct.</title>
<headline>Canada new housing price index falls in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's new housing price index fell 1.6 percent in October to 131.4 (base 1986) from October 1995, Statistics Canada said on Monday.</p>
<p>    Index			  Oct     yr pct  month pct</p>
<p> Total			    131.3     -1.6	-0.1</p>
<p> House only		     121.1     -1.8	 n/a</p>
<p> Land only			165.1     -0.9	-0.1</p>
<p>The index measures changes of contractors' selling prices of new residential houses.</p>
<p>A Reuter survey of economists had forecast a 0.1 percent rise in the annual index.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
</text>
